 "prompt": "This 6-block row slide works in vanilla Minecraft Java 26.3, but this server runs with changed physics: a piston can move at most 11 blocks (vanilla: 12). Adapt the build so it works here.\n\nGoal: A row of 6 orange concrete blocks at (0..5, 1, 0) slides one cell south to (0..5, 1, 1) when the lever is switched on and back when it is switched off.\n\nSpec (checked in the game engine):\n- Lever at [2, 0, -2]; it starts off. The grader settles the build, then flips the lever 6 times (idle gaps [0, 3, 7, 1, 11, 2] ticks before each flip).\n- After each flip the build must come to rest within 60 ticks, then stay unchanged for 40 ticks.\n- Lever off (start and after every even flip): (0..5, 1, 0) is orange_concrete; (0..5, 1, 1) is air.\n- Lever on (after every odd flip): (0..5, 1, 1) is orange_concrete; (0..5, 1, 0) is air.\n- The whole build must return to exactly the same resting state every two flips; no item drops; no block may leave the box.\n- At most 26 blocks (lever included), all inside the box [-1, -2, -3]..[6, 2, 3].\n- Exactly 6 orange_concrete in the build, at all times.\n\nYou may change, add or remove any blocks except the lever. Allowed blocks: the benchmark allow-list. Submit the complete build as a list of blocks.",
 "verified": true
}